Timber Run’s site cabin now reads between the first two decks in both the overview and jump views. One broadleaf and two pines frame the yard against open hills. The course geometry and the A15 beam and C7 respawn fixes are intact.

**Newcomer C retry — 19/20 wins across seeds 1–20.** All 20 races finished. On seed 12, the bot returned to the checkpoint and finished in 542 ticks, but slide mode ended before the beam. The attempt counted as a retry loss. [Ladder output](<C:/Users/kazda/kiro/third-life/.claude/worktrees/n19-parkour2/docs/shifts/2026-11-19-night/lanes/parkour/evidence/r2/ladder.log>)

**Plot edge — the yard blends into the village.** The dirt fades to grass before the fence. Three windowed angles showed continuous ground and no parkour tree or mesa spill. Both visitors reached the rim with zero blocked ticks. One default-loading run showed an empty gate before the course appeared at tick 378. The matched comparisons use blocking load, and the report preserves the late-build frame.

